 ## Overview
-This method provides a diagnostic visualization pipeline for neural volume models by rendering individual sample points as instanced spheres, colored by the network's predicted radiance and filtered by an opacity threshold [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard rendering methods by bypassing front-to-back compositing to inspect the raw distribution and magnitude of neural network outputs in 3D space, serving as a tool to verify that the implicit representation is capturing scene geometry and appearance correctly [S1, unofficial].
+This method provides a diagnostic visualization pipeline for neural volume models by rendering individual sample points as instanced spheres, colored by the network's predicted radiance and filtered by an opacity threshold [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard volume rendering by bypassing front-to-back compositing to inspect the raw distribution and magnitude of neural network outputs in 3D space [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs**
-*   **Input**: A dataset of rays associated with camera poses, a trained neural network model, and visualization parameters (empty threshold, number of samples per ray) [S1, unofficial].
