 *   **Output**: A 3D scene representation containing instanced sphere meshes representing non-empty samples, colored by predicted radiance [S1, unofficial].
 
 **Data Structures**
-*   **Ray Samples**: A tensor of shape `(num_rays, num_samples, 3)` containing 3D spatial coordinates $\mathbf{x}$ [S1, unofficial].
-*   **View Directions**: A tensor of shape `(num_rays, num_samples, 3)` containing viewing directions $\mathbf{d}$ (if the model is view-dependent) [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Ray Samples**: A tensor of positions $\mathbf{x}$ and optionally view directions $\mathbf{d}$ [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Model Output**: A tensor of shape `(batch, num_samples, 4)` containing raw predictions, split into color $\mathbf{c} \in \mathbb{R}^3$ and opacity $\sigma \in \mathbb{R}^1$ [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Instance Data**: A list or array of sphere meshes where each instance has a position, a base color (white or black), and a per-instance color attribute [S1, unofficial].
